      "body": "The issue is moot since this has been closed, but I'm afraid this still wouldn't have been useful. Your fix is unrelated to the test; it passes with or without it. It is good practice to always run your test scripts against affected versions, to confirm it reproduces the bug. Without that you don't know the test _works_.\n\nAlso note the bug in the OP is a `SIGBUS`, a fatal signal. It is completely expected that invalid operations like this raise exceptions, but it shouldn't be possible to trigger a fatal signal via the public API<sup>-ish. Terms and conditions apply. Offer void when `ctypes` or `mmap` or `gc` or various other low-level power tools.</sup>",
      "created_at": "2026-01-28T11:45:13Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-01-28T11:45:13Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/python/cpython/pull/144284#discussion_r2736259920",
